# Kerala PSC app — always-on rules

- Branch `psc-dev`, Firebase project `kerala-pcs-dev`. Read `CLAUDE.md` for conventions and `TASKS.md` for the current task. Work on one task ID at a time; keep changes inside its scope.
- Flutter commands always use FVM: `fvm flutter analyze`, `fvm flutter test`.
- Package name is `wordshool` (sic). Never rename it or the misspelled folders `resorces`, `repostiories`, `usercases`.
- Content collections are admin-only (written by Cloud Functions). Scores/XP/leaderboards are server-only.
- Firestore schema lives in `docs/firebase/FIREBASE_DESIGN.md` — update it in the same change when the schema changes.
- Never commit `.env*` (except `.env.example`), keys or service accounts.
- Before finishing: analyze + tests pass; tick the task card's "Done when" boxes; set board status to `review`.
- Don't commit until the user asks. When asked, commit `CW-0XX: ...` and push the task branch. No PRs.
